A||||8||88formula||2001 Toyota Tundra v8 vs 2002 Toyota Celica GT||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||10-05-2001||10:15 PM||||Was coming home from the restaurant and raced two cars with my truck from a stoplight. The first one was a late nineties Honda Civic with the trash can exhaust and who else knows for modifications, the rest of the car looked stock. From a stop we both took off about the same and raced until about 90 mph. By about 60 mph I had two Civic car lengths on him and keeped on pulling. Then a Toyota Celica GT decided to challenge me since he just witnessed me embarrass the civic. From the light we both launched about the same but this time by about 40 mph I pulled a car length on him and I maintained that lead up to again 90 mph. You could here his tires chirping in 1st-2nd-and 3rd gear as he rowed through the gears trying to pull ahead of a 4300 lb. pickup truck. <P>HA HA HA HA<P>This truck is faster than my formula was stock and will probably take my 3.4 on the highway. I love this 245 horsepower DOHC v8 with variable valve timing. The thing is a beast and can pull a big heavy pickup truck past these so called sports cars. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Luni420||10-06-2001||02:00 AM||||I have a 00 Celica GT and I believe you. My friend had a 97 Tacoma and he hung dead even with me until the high end, and I know a Tundra would do better than that. Id get ya on the freeway above 110 but up till then Id be lookin at truck tailights. Good kill.||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||10-06-2001||05:03 AM||||The GT-S celicas are actually pretty decent. 180bhp, 6-speed (god the motor and tranny that the MR-2 Spyder should have gotten!!!)<P>But the GT model is pretty slow.<P>That Toyota pickup is one of the best kept secrets in the auto world, they are bloody great fun with the monster DOHC motor.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steve Normington||10-06-2001||10:02 AM||||How does a Tacoma S-Runner (190 hp) stack up in this Toyota-thon? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||loafer87gt||10-06-2001||11:53 AM||||My Dad's Toyota truck hauls some serious ass. The previous owner pulled the 4 banger engine and swapped in a 3.4 from a newish Tacoma in there. It is a real sleeper truck, as looks like just a plain Toyota 1/4 tonne except for the rims and fat tires.||||reg||1
